WEBVTT

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.870
<v Callum Reid>Morning, all. Everyone on? Right, let's get going.</v>

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:14.599
<v Sarah Okafor>I'm here. Still no coffee, though. That broken coffee machine in the canteen is properly testing my patience.</v>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.190
<v Jamie Brennan>Probably doing your blood pressure a favour.</v>

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:22.719
<v Sarah Okafor>You'd think. Having the opposite effect, actually.</v>

00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:28.929
<v David Whitfield>I'm just hoping the weather sorts itself out for the weekend. Supposed to be going camping.</v>

00:00:31.379 --> 00:00:32.579
<v Marcus Hale>In April? Brave.</v>

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.299
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, that's one word for it. Forecast changes every time I look.</v>

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:45.619
<v Callum Reid>Right, before we get the full shipping forecast, quick round of where we're at.</v>

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:51.039
<v Priya Raman>Yep. Tested the relief valve yesterday and it's all fine now. That's sorted.</v>

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.950
<v Callum Reid>Lovely, cheers.</v>

00:00:55.409 --> 00:01:00.310
<v Jamie Brennan>I've swapped the filter on the power pack on one as well. All done.</v>

00:01:02.159 --> 00:01:03.359
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Nice one.</v>

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:09.370
<v Marcus Hale>And my visit to Tollgate with the contractor, that's done. All signed off.</v>

00:01:10.189 --> 00:01:11.390
<v Callum Reid>Good, thanks.</v>

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:18.049
<v Callum Reid>I've got the downtime for the little water valve on two agreed with production. Scheduling's sorted.</v>

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:27.750
<v David Whitfield>On the risk assessment for the little water valve on two, I've got the first half done. Working through the rest of it.</v>

00:01:29.319 --> 00:01:30.519
<v Priya Raman>Yep, with you.</v>

00:01:32.819 --> 00:01:41.219
<v David Whitfield>The jam clearance and sensor checks on the Main Outfeed Conveyor, though—I can't get on with those. Waiting on the permit to be signed.</v>

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.760
<v Callum Reid>Ah, right. Understood.</v>

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:52.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Pricey asked me to pass on that the near-miss write-up for the door switch on two is about halfway through.</v>

00:01:55.359 --> 00:01:58.159
<v Hannah Price>Cheers. Sorry, was fighting the mute button there.</v>

00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:03.000
<v Callum Reid>You're coming through now. Right, new stuff this morning.</v>

00:02:04.019 --> 00:02:09.969
<v Marcus Hale>We've got a pressure drop on the Boiler Feedwater Pump. That's the main thing from my end.</v>

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:16.710
<v Callum Reid>Hannah, can you investigate the pressure drop on the Boiler Feedwater Pump? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.159
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll investigate it. Understood on the urgency.</v>

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:27.110
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, you clipped out for me. Which pump was that?</v>

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.629
<v Callum Reid>Boiler Feedwater Pump. Hannah's taking the pressure-drop investigation.</v>

00:02:31.539 --> 00:02:34.689
<v Hannah Price>Yep, that's mine. Everything else aside for that one.</v>

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:36.979
<v Callum Reid>Thanks.</v>

00:02:38.139 --> 00:02:46.189
<v David Whitfield>While we're on pressure—just an observation—I saw the pressure on the Stretch Wrapper dip for a few minutes. Came back on its own.</v>

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.590
<v Marcus Hale>Oh, it recovered by itself?</v>

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.610
<v David Whitfield>Yeah. Nothing outstanding from that, just what I saw.</v>

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.990
<v Callum Reid>Okay, cheers for the heads-up.</v>

00:02:55.819 --> 00:03:00.370
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll recalibrate the sensors on the heater box on one at half two.</v>

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.729
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Half two, boss? Sorry, someone was talking outside here.</v>

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, at half two.</v>

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:14.310
<v Priya Raman>I heard half two as well. Not just your headset this time.</v>

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:21.659
<v Callum Reid>And I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the line 2 guard for Monday.</v>

00:03:22.199 --> 00:03:23.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Monday for that, Reidy?</v>

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:28.909
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, Monday. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:31.259 --> 00:03:32.460
<v Marcus Hale>Right, got you.</v>

00:03:34.789 --> 00:03:39.340
<v Jamie Brennan>There's also the purchase order for the IM1 hydraulic unit that needs chasing.</v>

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:46.360
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll chase the purchase order for the IM1 hydraulic unit tomorrow. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:49.520
<v Jamie Brennan>Cheers, Saz.</v>

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:55.740
<v Sarah Okafor>No worries. At least I can read that one on my screen without squinting.</v>

00:03:56.229 --> 00:03:59.030
<v Jamie Brennan>That's because I've finally made the font bigger.</v>

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:04.500
<v Callum Reid>A genuine improvement, then. Anything else new we need in this morning?</v>

00:04:05.509 --> 00:04:07.259
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Nothing else from me, no.</v>

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:09.800
<v Priya Raman>No, that's me as well.</v>

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.740
<v Hannah Price>All clear here. I can hear everyone now, at least.</v>

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.000
<v Marcus Hale>Nothing more from my side.</v>

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:21.850
<v David Whitfield>Nor mine. I'll spare you the rest of the forecast.</v>

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.959
<v Callum Reid>Much appreciated. Right, thanks everyone. Leave it there.</v>

00:04:26.279 --> 00:04:27.480
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, all.</v>
